<title>USA: Pfizer's Zoloft approved as OCD treatment.</title>
<headline>Pfizer's Zoloft approved as OCD treatment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pfizer Inc said it received regulatory approval from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market its drug Zoloft for treatment of obsessive compulsive disorder (OCD).</p>
<p>Zoloft had already been approved as a depression treatment.  </p>
<p>Zoloft had worldwide sales of $965 million in the first nine months of 1996, up from $754 million in the same period a year ago.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
